So hey, let's get started, shall we

93
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Music?

94
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
It was our first night out. camping

95
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Went all through the troop.

96
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Everyone was stirring.

97
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,000
What a loud happy group.

98
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:47,000
The tents were all pitched and the fire was lit,

99
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:52,000
but the scouts sang their songs and each patrol did a skit.

100
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Soon they were nestled, all snug in their beds

101
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:59,000
as visions of instant oatmeal danced in their heads.

102
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:03,000
The scouters and neckerchiefs, silence and ploughing

103
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:07,000
had settled ourselves for a long winter's snoring

104
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Music.

105
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Out on the campsite, there arose such a clatter.

106
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:22,000
I unzipped my sleeping bag. to see what was the matter,

107
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:27,000
I crawled to the door and put on my cap, unzipped the tent

108
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,000
and looked out. the flap,

109
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:32,000
The moon on the carpet of leaves on the ground

110
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:35,000
gave a luster of midday. as I looked around,

111
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:39,000
when what then appeared to my initial survey

112
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:44,000
was eight tiny raccoons and a miniature sleigh

113
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:48,000
with a big hulking driver, all covered in hair,

114
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,000
I knew in a moment it must be a bear.

115
00:07:51,000 --> 00:08:01,000
Music,

116
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Silent and stealthy, his raccoons. they came,

117
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:07,000
as he growled and grunted and called them by a name,

118
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Now Nasher, now Chewer, now Masher, and Eater

119
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:15,000
on gorger, on nibbler, on scarfer and feeder,

120
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:19,000
To the picnic table in the cooler, with no time of wasting.

121
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:23,000
the food these scouts brought is ours for the tasting,

122
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:26,000
As leaves that, before the wild hurricane, fly,

123
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
when they meet with an obstacle, mount up to the sky,

124
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,000
so up to the coolers, his raccoons. they flew

125
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:36,000
and filled their sleigh and their fat bellies too.

126
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
I thrust out my head and I made a loud sound.

127
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:43,000
everything stopped and the bear turned around.

128
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:50,000
Music,

129
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
He was covered in fur, from his head to his paw

130
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:57,000
and his coat shown in the moonlight as he opened his maw,

131
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:02,000
his eyes, how they glowed, his teeth, how keen

132
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:06,000
and the claws on his paws were the longest I've seen.

133
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:09,000
Half a bagel was tight clenched in his teeth

134
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:13,000
and the package encircled his head like a wreath.

135
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
He had a broad face and a giant round belly

136
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
that shook when he growled like a bowl full of jelly.

137
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:22,000
He gazed straight at me and he said:

138
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:25,000
look here, we'll leave you plenty,

139
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
but one night a year we get a few goodies

140
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,000
for our cubs and kits.

141
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:33,000
We'll leave the ramen noodles and other sundry bags

142
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Music.

143
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,000
A wink of his eye and a twist of his head

144
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:46,000
suit gave me to know I had nothing to dread.

145
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:50,000
He sprang to his sleigh to his team, gave a growl

146
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:54,000
and away. they all flew stealthy as a barn owl,

147
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,000
But I heard him exclaim as he flew into the woods:

148
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
be prepared next time, scouts,

149
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
and thanks for the goods

